  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 121 AM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nTuesday night through Saturday\nAssessment...a certainty (>95%) of a cool down. Medium (40-60%)\nconfidence regarding rain chances.\n\nA developing tropical connection with the Gulf and the remnants of \nRachel will bring surges of moisture into the area; the first \nTuesday night into Wednesday and the second around Thursday.\n\nTrends with the models are shunting the first surge of moisture to \nthe south and east of the area due to a frontal passage that \noccurred Monday night. Thus there is a very real possibility that \nTuesday night/Wednesday may end up being dry for much of the area.\n\nThe moisture surge centered around Thursday is stronger so this may \nend up being the better chance for rain. The model consensus has a\n55-70 percent chance for rain centered around Thursday.\n\nA more significant cold front will sweep through the area Friday \nnight bringing below normal temperatures for next weekend. \nAlthough the global models have backed off a little with the \ncolder temperatures, the prospects for the first frost appear to\nbe on the increase especially north of I-80.",
